course: dictionary
lesson: 6682
title: Observatory: a place for watching the sky
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An observatory is a building where people watch and study the sky, using big telescopes and other instruments. Look at the words around it to find its meaning: stars, planets and space are the clues. «Rubin Observatory in Chile released its first images in 2025.» Images are pictures, so this observatory took pictures of space.
explain: Observatories are built on high, dry, dark places, away from city lights, because the sky is clearer there. You can see this in the phrase «the Royal Observatory», which tells you it is a famous place where the sky is studied.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The red time ball at the Royal Observatory, Greenwich, has dropped at 1 pm every day since 1833 so ships could set their clocks.» If you put "a building for watching space" in place of "observatory", the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: An observatory is a building with big telescopes and instruments for watching and studying stars, planets and space.
fact: Some observatories are for watching the weather, earthquakes, birds or other natural things.
fact: The Royal Observatory at Greenwich is where the Prime Meridian, 0° longitude, runs.
fact: «The red time ball at the Royal Observatory, Greenwich, has dropped at 1 pm every day since 1833 so ships could set their clocks.»
fact: Famous observatories include Mauna Kea in Hawaii and the observatories in the Chilean desert.
exercise: What is the main job of an observatory? | *Watching and studying stars, planets and space | Baking bread for the town | Selling telescopes in a shop | Growing tall trees
exercise: Why are observatories built on high, dry, dark places? | To keep the telescopes warm in the sun | *So the sky is clearer, away from city lights | Because the ground there is soft | To be near busy shops
exercise: «Rubin Observatory in Chile released its first images in 2025.» What country is the Rubin Observatory in? | Scotland | *Chile | Australia | Hawaii
test: «The red time ball at the Royal Observatory, Greenwich, has dropped at 1 pm every day since 1833.» Find and copy the word that means fell down. | ships | *dropped | clocks | ball
test: A weather observatory is a place for what? | Sailing ships | *Watching and recording the weather | Baking cakes | Playing football
exam: Which sentence best describes an observatory? | A ship for sailing across the sea | A shop that sells telescopes | *A building with big telescopes and instruments for watching space | A park with tall trees
